  "rawMarkdown": "\nLet A and B be two sets. Then,\nA is a **subset** of B if all elements of A appear in B\n\t$A \\subsetneq B$\n\tA can have as many elements as B or less, and they all appear in B\n\t$A = \\{1,2\\},  B = \\{1,2,3\\}$\n\t$A = \\{1,2,3\\}, B = \\{1,2,3\\}$\n\n$A$ is a $Proper Subset$ of $B$ if $A$ strictly has less elements than $B$, and they all exist in $B$.\n\t$A \\subset B$\n\t$A = \\{1,2,3\\}, B = \\{1,2,3\\}$\n\n\n",
